    "https://lyon.isolvedhire.com/jobs/1838265": {
      "title": "Resource Sharing Librarian",
      "description": "Resource Sharing Librarian - Batesville, AR - Lyon College Jobs Jobs Login Back to all jobs Resource Sharing Librarian Posted 07-Aug-2026 (CST) Batesville, AR, USA 40,000-43,000 per year Salary Full Time Email Me Similar Jobs Email Me This Job Resource Sharing Librarian One Role, a World of Impact Lyon College is looking for a versatile, energetic librarian to lead our resource sharing program and help shape how our campus community discovers, accesses, and preserves information. This isn't a one-note job - you'll move between reference desk, archives, classroom, and social media feed, all in the same week. At Lyon, you won't be a cog in a giant system. You'll be a visible, valued member of a close-knit library team where your ideas actually shape how we serve our campus. Small college, big impact! What You'll Do Provide research and reference services across print and digital resources, working directly with faculty, staff, and students in a range of subject areas Manage Interlibrary Loan (ILL) operations, including creating clear, helpful materials that promote ILL services to the campus Bring our online presence to life through social media and polished, user-friendly LibGuides Build surveys, tutorials, forms, and other communications using Google services, LibWizard, and other library tools Steward our ContentDM digital archives and the College's physical archival collections Teach library instruction sessions as needed Supervise and mentor student workers Lead outreach efforts on and off campus through programming, information sharing, and community connections Contribute to library data collection and help shape library policy Take on other duties as assigned by the Library Director - because no two days here look exactly alike What You Bring MLS/MLIS from an ALA-accredited program (or equivalent experience) Comfort with ILL platforms and eagerness to learn tools like LibGuides, LibWizard, ContentDM, and Google Workspace A natural communicator who's just as comfortable drafting a tutorial as posting on social media Interest in archives and special collections Strong organizational skills and enjoyment of mentoring student staff A collaborative spirit and genuine passion for removing barriers between people and information About Lyon College Lyon College is a selective private liberal arts college affiliated with the Presbyterian Church (U.S.A.) in the historic town of Batesville, Arkansas. Home to more than 660 students from 30 states and 18 countries, the College is renowned for its inclusive and nurturing academic community. Batesville, with a population of 11,000, was named the Best City to Live in Arkansas by USA Today. It offers a safe, vibrant environment and is a regional hub for commercial, medical, and social activities. Why Lyon? At Lyon, we prioritize excellent teaching, inclusive environments, and the persistence and success of our students and faculty. We support innovative teaching, meaningful research, and professional development in a close-knit academic community. Our liberal arts foundation encourages students to think critically about their place in the world and explore diverse perspectives. Equal Opportunity Employer Lyon College does not discriminate based on race, color, religion, gender, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. We comply with all federal and state laws regarding equal employment opportunities. Learn more about Lyon College at www.lyon.edu . Join us at Lyon College and be the difference in shaping th e future of curiou s and dedicated students! Full Job Description Apply now How would you like to verify your identity? Continue with phone Verify with a one-time text code Continue with email Verify with a one-time code Powered by iSolved Talent Acquisition Sign Up For Job Alerts! Name You must type a name. Email You must type a valid email. Location (city, state or zip code) You must select a location. Accept Terms of Service I agree to the terms